# The Docker-in-Docker image that Luther's fabric-peer Helm chart runs beside
# the peer to build and run Docker chaincode (luthersystems/mars).
#
# It is docker:dind with the eMudhra (emSign) roots removed, so dockerd does
# not trust them when it pulls images. Alpine's ca-certificates in the
# upstream image still trusts all four, and eight eMudhra intermediates were
# compromised (CVE-2026-111943). It keeps the upstream user, and its
# entrypoint runs the upstream one.
#
# DIND_VERSION is the newest Docker that Fabric 2.5's peer can use. The
# chart used docker:stable-dind, frozen at the end-of-life 19.03.14 since
# 2020 (#159). The peer builds chaincode images with API 1.25 (POST
# /v1.25/build). Docker 29 refuses that version, and with
# DOCKER_MIN_API_VERSION=1.24 its classic builder panics after the build: a
# nil *AuxFormatter is stored in the AuxEmitter interface, so the nil check in
# emitImageID passes (moby daemon/builder/dockerfile/builder.go). Docker 28
# keeps the concrete type. On 28.5.2 a Fabric 2.5.7 peer installs, upgrades
# and runs Go chaincode. Do not move to Docker 29 until moby fixes that.
#
# dind-entrypoint.sh lets this image start on a /var/lib/docker volume that
# Docker 19.03 wrote; see that script.
ARG DIND_VERSION=28.5.2
FROM docker:${DIND_VERSION}-dind

# Alpine fixes reach the upstream image only when Docker releases, so take
# them here (zlib 1.3.2-r1 fixed a HIGH CVE in 29.9.2-dind; 28.5.2-dind is older).
RUN apk upgrade --no-cache

COPY dind-entrypoint.sh /usr/local/bin/dind-entrypoint.sh
ENTRYPOINT ["dind-entrypoint.sh"]
# Harden the image with the build-harden kit (images/harden): today it makes
# the image trust no CA in harden/policy/ca-distrust.list (the eMudhra roots
# and intermediates whose keys leaked, CVE-2026-111943). Keep this after the
# last package install; the kit is bind-mounted, so no kit file stays.
RUN --mount=type=bind,source=harden,target=/harden sh /harden/harden.sh
